## Commands

Shared commands live at `/mnt/torus/projects/.cursor/commands/` (inherited by all workspaces via parent-directory traversal). Workspace-specific commands stay here.

### Shared (from parent — available in all workspaces)

Generic: `ask`, `apply-ask`, `ask-http`, `prompt-code-responsibility-check`
Workflow: `review`, `apply-review`, `review-prompt`, `commit`, `create-implementation-plan`, `implement-plan`, `verify-implementation`, `create-phase-chain`
Packet-pattern review: `diff-review`, `diff-review-mcp`, `diff-review-apply`, `review-plan`, `review-arch-doc`
Knowledge: `journal-entry`, `insight`, `vision`, `todo`
Docs: `doc-check`, `check-doc-opportunities`

Many shared commands load `@{name}_ws.mdc` if it exists for workspace-specific extensions.

## Prompt-Facing Invariants

`.cursor/invariants/` contains compact markdown invariant blocks for tools and
frontier prompts. Cursor rules remain canonical; invariant files are
repo-relative prompt inputs.

| File | Used by |
|---|---|
| `modularize.md` | `scripts/modularize plan` default `--invariants-file` |
| `review.md` | Review and diff-review handoff packets |
| `handoff.md` | Agent-to-agent packet construction |

### Workspace-Specific (gateway only)

Consult: `consult-plan`, `consult-implement`, `consult-review`, `consult-research`, `consult-architect`
Pipeline: `pipeline-refine`, `docstring-enhance`, `modularize`
Quality: `overhaul`, `overhaul-file`, `review-phase`, `check-redundancy_ws`

